{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Pod1Ha7XpXnD9izYJKZwyU", "type": "tool_result", "content": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e549a876-c919-4b69-9331-00c0229ab3a3", "uuid": "4bd66ecb-f61b-42ff-ad6b-bdf26a144d2b", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:34:57.803Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Pod1Ha7XpXnD9izYJKZwyU", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
